      "titulo": "The rule",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "A few nouns can be **masculine or feminine** with the **same meaning**. Which one people use depends on the region, the register, or just the speaker."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "tabla",
          "encabezados": [
            "Noun",
            "Notes"
          ],
          "filas": [
            [
              "el / la sartén",
              "In Mexico, **el sartén** is very common."
            ],
            [
              "el / la mar",
              "**El mar** is general; **la mar** is poetic, or used by fishermen and sailors."
            ],
            [
              "el / la azúcar",
              "Both are heard; **la azúcar** is common in parts of Latin America."
            ],
            [
              "el / la calor",
              "**El calor** is standard; **la calor** is regional and casual."
            ],
            [
              "el / la tilde",
              "**La tilde** is more common."
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Whichever gender you choose, keep the adjectives and articles **consistent**: **un sartén limpio** or **una sartén limpia**, never mixed."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Tip: pick a side and stay on it. Mixing genders in one phrase is the only real mistake."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
